e pregnancy but  then it was kind of weird cuz they had  me pee in the cup and then she gave me  an ultrasound anyway and we weren't  expecting an ultrasound because I didn't  think they did it at six weeks so I'm  kind of bummed that Matt didn't get to  be there even though it was literally a  blob but I got to see the little heart  beating beating it's there and it just  it made it so real to me seeing its  heart beating just you know made me feel  like everything was okay and everything  was good I'm really excited I got to see  my little baby today makes it all worth  it all right  decided enough so typically people wait  until the second trimester to tell  anybody that they're pregnant just to  make sure that everything's okay but for  me I was 29 I've had two perfectly  normal pregnancies two healthy kids so I  decided to tell a few close people okay  so alex is coming over for those of you  who don't know she is one of my best  friends and I'm not quite ready to tell  everybody but I'm going to tell her  because she's gonna be so excited okay  oh my gosh what what do you touch to  anything are you pregnant  oh I decided to tell Alex first and  foremost because she comes to my house  almost every weekend and we always have  a glass of wine and she would know  within five minutes if I'm not drinking  wine there's a reason so because this  was my last pregnancy to do everything  right I started planning there were a  few things that I decided I absolutely  needed to do one of which was a  maternity photoshoot so I ordered a  dress which in hindsight is so stupid to  start doing it that early as well as  daily photos of my boat because I never  got any photos of my bump and at that  time in my mind there was not an inkling  of a thought that anything would go  wrong so one evening out of nowhere I  just got these bizarre flu-like symptoms  oh man it's like that crippling nose you  know Neil I can't think about anything  morning sickness isn't actually morning  sickness it can happen at any time  so I took that as a good sign of things  are happening things are progressing you  know so at this point if you don't want  to hear any of the more medical details  of what happened uh skip ahead to this  time in the video so the next morning I  woke up and when I stood up from bed  there was this little pop it was like in  at the base of my uterus almost like a  little just blip with that came a little  bit of pink colored fluid I think that's  fairly normal you usually don't get  concerned until there's bright red blood  but it was weird you know I didn't  really think anything of it and I went  to work and throughout the day at work I  just started feeling worse and worse I I  started to bleed  a little bit at work and then it got a  little worse so I have been spotting um  I started spotting yesterday but it was  like not that bad  today as the day went on it I I noticed  it just slowly started and be more and  it was getting more red in color and so  now I'm and I'm waiting and my mom and  I'm gonna go to the emergency room cuz  my doctor told me to and it's it's like  pouring blood no there's no way I can  fathom that I'm still pregnant hey  there's no way I feel wrong like  documenting this it just I really don't  want to like talk to anybody I wish  someone had talked to me about this so  not stayed with the kids and I went with  my mom to the ER and I got there and it  was very crowded and I waited in the  waiting room for hours by that point I  had started bleeding very heavily I just  remember feeling so embarrassed and  nervous that I was going to get blood  all over my pants so they finally called  me back and turns out they didn't have a  room for me  they had parked a bed next to the  elevator in the hallway I wait I waited  and not bed by the elevator  um I a physician's assistant she asked  me some questions and I was just like  get me out of here I don't want to be  here but at this but I honestly even  asked any questions through this entire  process because I was totally in shock  so they finally wheeled me to get an  ultrasound they did that and they  wheeled me back up and finally a  physician's assistant came and sat next  to me starts reading out loud that I  have no longer pregnant and I knew I was  just trying not to cry and I didn't want  her to keep talking to me she kept  talking about stuff showing me pictures  and shown and I was just like I don't  care oh I wanted to say it I didn't say  that but like in my mind I was like just  nod so she leaves just saying okay okay  okay so I could get out of there when I  got home it was so late because I had  been there for hours and hours so I was  exhausted so after four hours I found  out that I'm not pregnant anymore and  that's I don't know why you cry  like I I saw it I saw it's a heartbeat  and I wanna know what happened  hey I want to know what I did wrong I  don't remember saying that I'm a very  logical person and I need answers  I kept thinking like maybe if I had just  taken it easy after I felt sick that  night maybe if I had gone into work  maybe I you know I took on too much or I  was I was too stressed or I I I needed  to find a reason why and the difficult  part to grasp is that there's no reason  why to this day I still can't shake and  I know it's fully irrational but I still  can't shake the feeling of like well I'm  not supposed to have a third kid and  this was my side so I hope that comes  when it goes away at some point you know  you didn't do anything no not yet  so it's no the second day um since the  yardie day - since the ER woke up in the  night last night with horrible cramps at  like 2:00 in the morning and a migraine  and I couldn't fall back asleep till  like 5:00 so the recovery process took  about two weeks I was bleeding I was  tired  it takes a toll physically and it's it's  very intense it was a blur cuz I went  back to work you know it's not this  thing you can call out sick for for two  weeks cuz it's not something anyone  talks about I just pushed it to the back  of my mind and continued on with my life  also I I have two kids life doesn't stop  I mean just because I went through that  doesn't mean that life stops for me and  they don't have my existing  responsibilities which I think helps  I have not cried today and that is an  accomplishment because if you know me  you know I cry about everything I was  very sad and I felt very stupid I felt  very stupid for just assuming that  everything was okay and everything was  gonna be okay and I could make all these  plans and tell people and buy stuff and  I felt confused about why I didn't see  it coming and why I didn't know what to  look for the thing that has bothered me  the most is that there's no conversation  around this it's not until it happens to  you and you find certain support groups  and people and stuff that that  conversation even comes up I would have  given anything to have just a little  insight a little inkling into what to  look out for so I would HIGHLY encourage  you whether you're pregnant or not or  thinking about it or not or maybe your  your partner is pregnant whatever it may  be please do some research you can go to  this website or you can check any of the  links in the description as of right now  I can't even fathom thinking about you  know trying again or having another  trying for another but at least I'm kind  of at peace with it  with most stories of miscarriage or when  people choose to share their experience  it has a happy ending  well my happy ending I guess is that I  already have two amazing kids and for  now I'm super happy with that and I'm  not saying that I'm ruling anything out  in the future but I'm just saying for  right now I'm not putting any pressure  on myself and I I'm lucky to be able to  make that choice because I know that a  lot of people don't get that luxury so  since that has happened I am still asked  daily if I'm going to have another c